<title>INDIA: Indian banks asked to apply for gold imports.</title>
<headline>Indian banks asked to apply for gold imports.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India on Monday invited banks seeking to import gold, silver and platimum to apply to the central bank for approval.</p>
<p>It said eligibility criteria had been outlined in the 1997/2000 Export Import Policy set by the federal government.</p>
<p>Applications should detail arrangements planned by the bank to undertake transactions in these metals, RBI said.</p>
<p>Applications are to be made to the chief general manager, department of banking operations and development, RBI central office at World Trade Centre at Cuffe Parade, Bombay.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
